---
export const title = 'Multiple selection';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  With <code>selection="multiple"</code> every item shows a checkbox that <kbd>Space</kbd> or a
  click toggles. Checking an item checks its descendants; an item is checked when all its children
  are, and indeterminate (<code>aria-checked="mixed"</code>) when only some are. Disabled items
  keep their state and are skipped by the cascade.
</p>
<p>
  As on <code>wc-listbox</code> and <code>wc-select</code>, <code>value</code> is a
  comma-separated list and <code>values</code> the same as an array, so item values must not
  contain commas. They list every checked item, parents included. A value set from code is
  normalized: listing a parent checks its children.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-tree
    id='tree-permissions-demo'
    label='Permissions'
    selection='multiple'
    value='users.read,billing'
    style='width: min(100%, 22rem);'
  >
    <wc-tree-item value='users' label='Users' expanded>
      <wc-icon slot='start' name='group'></wc-icon>
      <wc-tree-item value='users.read' label='View users'></wc-tree-item>
      <wc-tree-item value='users.invite' label='Invite users'></wc-tree-item>
      <wc-tree-item value='users.remove' label='Remove users'></wc-tree-item>
    </wc-tree-item>
    <wc-tree-item value='billing' label='Billing' expanded>
      <wc-icon slot='start' name='payments'></wc-icon>
      <wc-tree-item value='billing.invoices' label='View invoices'></wc-tree-item>
      <wc-tree-item value='billing.plan' label='Change plan'></wc-tree-item>
    </wc-tree-item>
    <wc-tree-item value='admin' label='Administration'>
      <wc-icon slot='start' name='shield'></wc-icon>
      <wc-tree-item value='admin.audit' label='Audit log'></wc-tree-item>
      <wc-tree-item value='admin.sso' label='Single sign-on' disabled></wc-tree-item>
    </wc-tree-item>
  </wc-tree>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#tree-permissions-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change', event.detail.values.join(', '));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
